# Wave W17-V (Route 205): gale pine — a ridge pine with a wind-bent crown: tiered and full, its tiers leaning east under the valley wind that turns the Galeworks turbines above the road, highlight lifted clear of the turf, on gale turf (ground baked in). Route 205’s own tree — the fleet’s only bent pine: split from Route 203’s upright dusted coal pine by the lean itself (wind vs smoke) and from Route 206’s shadow pine by register (open ridge vs pillar shade).
